    "CustomerSummary": "This case does not identify specific customers but refers to retail investors generally who received inaccurate Form CRS disclosures from Parsonex Capital Markets. The firm failed to disclose that several of its financial professionals had legal or disciplinary history, and later failed to update its Form CRS to disclose that its control affiliate had disciplinary history. The firm also omitted required language regarding conflicts of interest and fee disclosures. This case does not involve a Care Obligation violation but rather violations of Exchange Act § 17(a)(1), Exchange Act Rule 17a-14, and FINRA Rule 2010 related to Form CRS disclosure requirements.",
    "OverallSummary": "This case involves Parsonex Capital Markets, a broker-dealer that primarily acts as a managing dealer or placement agent for private placements offered to retail investors. The firm willfully violated Exchange Act § 17(a)(1), Exchange Act Rule 17a-14, and FINRA Rule 2010 by filing and delivering to customers a Form CRS (Customer Relationship Summary) that omitted required information from June 30, 2020, to February 9, 2023. Specifically, the firm failed to disclose that four of its registered representatives had legal or disciplinary history. After February 9, 2023, the firm updated its Form CRS but then failed to further update it after March 13, 2023, when its control affiliate (an investment adviser) entered into a cease-and-desist order with the SEC. The firm also omitted required language regarding conflicts of interest and fee disclosures from its Form CRS. This case does not involve Care Obligation violations under Reg BI, but rather violations related to Form CRS disclosure requirements. The firm was censured, fined $10,000, and required to undertake remediation of its Form CRS deficiencies. No specific information about customer losses or impacts was provided in the document."
